prompt: Wide 15th-century Đại Việt rebel army camp in the forested Lam Sơn hills at night; a scholar sits small and off-center at about one-fifth frame height inside an open bamboo-and-thatch command shelter writing on a scroll by lamplight, Vietnamese soldiers in lacquered leather armor with rattan shields and spears sharpen blades around campfires, war elephants stand among the trees, smoke drifts up into the jungle canopy, plain solid-crimson cloth banners, no emblem or lettering, lean against the posts. No Ming/Qing Chinese, Japanese, Nguyễn-dynasty or European elements.
